{
  "_id": "index-nephi-3",
  "content": [
    {
      "text": "eldest son of Nephi2, given charge of plates, 3 Ne. 1:2. sorrows for wickedness of people, 3 Ne. 1:10. cries unto the Lord in behalf of his people, 3 Ne. 1:11–12. hears voice of the Lord, sign of Christ’s birth to be given, 3 Ne. 1:12–13. performs baptisms, 3 Ne. 1:23. makes record on plates of Nephi1, 3 Ne. 5:9–10. was visited by angels and voice of the Lord, 3 Ne. 7:15, 18. ministers with great power, 3 Ne. 7:17. casts out devils, raises brother from dead, 3 Ne. 7:19 (19:4). arouses people’s anger because of many miracles, 3 Ne. 7:20. Jesus calls Nephi forward, 3 Ne. 11:18–20. is given power to baptize, 3 Ne. 11:21–22 (12:1). is called by Jesus to minister as one of twelve disciples, 3 Ne. 19:4. is baptized, baptizes other eleven disciples, 3 Ne. 19:11–12. is told to bring forth records, 3 Ne. 23:7–8. is commanded to write missing parts of record, 3 Ne. 23:9–13.",
